{
  "title": "Import jobs hard-fail when OPENROUTER_API_KEY is unset, before \
save_recipe runs",
  "description": "build_registry in server/src/scraping/runner.rs calls \
CachingAiClient::from_env()? while constructing the step registry, so with \
OPENROUTER_API_KEY unset every import/scrape job fails before any step — \
including save_recipe — executes. This is inconsistent with the design of the \
AI steps themselves: every auto-enrichment step is continues_on_failure and \
runs after save_recipe, so an *invalid* key imports recipes fine (enrichments \
fail soft) while a *missing* key imports nothing. This is why the iOS CI \
database had zero recipes: the workflow set no key, the seed CLI reported \
success (it only sees job enqueue), and the old vacuous UI test hid the empty \
list. The iOS workflow now works around it with a dummy OPENROUTER_API_KEY. \
Decide the intended behavior: either defer AI client construction to the \
enrich steps (missing key behaves like invalid key: recipe saves, enrichments \
fail soft), or fail fast at server startup when auto-enrichments are \
configured but the key is missing, so misconfiguration is loud instead of \
per-job and silent from the importer's perspective.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "server",
    "pipeline",
    "ci",
  ],
